sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User
    participant I as Interaction Agent
    participant R as Task Registry<br/>and Search
    participant Q as Shared Durable<br/>Queue
    participant W as Execution<br/>Workers
    participant S as Durable<br/>Memory
    participant T as Gmail and<br/>Task Tools

    Note over I,S: Optimization: retrieve relevant saved tasks, bound model history, and cap work in flight.<br/>Shown limits are configurable defaults for one backend process.

    rect rgb(239, 246, 255)
        Note over I,R: 1. Bound discovery instead of injecting the full agent roster
        U->>I: Request work
        alt Stable task ID or conversation link is known
            I->>R: Resolve the saved task identity
        else Discover a relevant saved task
            I->>R: Search by keywords, meaning and identifiers
            R-->>I: Up to 30 compact candidates, 10 per page
        end
        I->>R: Inspect task identity and current version
        R-->>I: Verified stable ID, version and state
        Note over I,R: Clarify ambiguous identities before dispatch.<br/>Create explicitly only after archive-inclusive discovery.
    end

    rect rgb(255, 247, 237)
        Note over Q,W: 2. Bound execution through one shared chat and reminder queue
        loop Each task submitted for this request
            I->>Q: Enqueue inspected ID, version and instructions
            alt Fewer than 100 waiting jobs
                Q->>Q: Persist queued job and request-group membership
            else Queue is full
                Q->>Q: Persist rejected terminal outcome
            end
        end
        I->>Q: Seal request group when submissions finish
        Note over Q,W: Workers may start before sealing; sealing gates final delivery.<br/>At most 4 active jobs, one per task; start oldest runnable work.<br/>Expire after 5 minutes waiting; runtime timeout is 300 seconds.
        loop Accepted jobs; up to 4 workers run in parallel
            Q->>W: Claim job when a worker slot and task are free
            W->>S: Load bounded task history
            S-->>W: State, summary and recent complete exchanges<br/>within 8,000 estimated history tokens
            loop At most 8 tool iterations
                W->>S: Journal tool intent before effects
                W->>T: Execute tool
                T-->>W: Tool outcome
                W->>S: Preserve full result or artifact
                opt Exact older details are needed
                    W->>S: Retrieve cited source or bounded excerpt
                    S-->>W: Original evidence on demand
                end
            end
            W-->>Q: Persist succeeded, failed or interrupted outcome
        end
        Note over Q,W: Restart resumes unexpired queued jobs.<br/>Safe read-only failures permit at most one automatic retry per request.<br/>Attempted writes or unknown tools require review; uncertain actions are not automatically replayed.
    end

    rect rgb(240, 253, 244)
        Note over I,Q: 3. Consolidate results instead of sending one update per worker
        Q-->>I: Deliver once group is sealed and all members are terminal
        Note over I,Q: Rejected, expired, failed and interrupted jobs also count.
        I-->>U: One grouped update with outcomes or required review
    end
